#25_Speed_Test_Mixed_Paragraph
Typing is a skill that grows with regular practice. Sit up straight, relax your shoulders, and keep your fingers on the home row. Look at the screen, not at the keys, and type each word with a steady rhythm. At first, accuracy matters more than speed; fix your mistakes and your speed will follow. Practise for 15 minutes a day, and in 30 days you could type 40 words per minute, maybe more! Don't give up: every expert was once a beginner.
